Falsifies `machine_discovery::acpi::verification::the_dmar_walk_terminates_and_stays_inside_the_body`.

The defect: the DMAR's minimum structure length becomes two, which is the MADT's
minimum one table over. The two walks look alike and are not: a MADT entry is a
one-byte type and a one-byte length, while a DMAR remapping structure is a
little-endian `u16` type and a `u16` length, so its own header is four bytes. A
structure claiming a length of two or three advances the cursor inside its own
header, and the next iteration re-reads the second half of this structure as the
first half of the next one, forever.

This is the parity failure AGENTS.md rule 5 names, in miniature: a constant copied
across from the sibling implementation that is correct there and wrong here. The
file's tests write a zero length and nothing else, so they stay green.

Expected to fail: `assert!(it.at >= last + 4)`.

diff --git a/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs b/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs
--- a/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs
+++ b/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs
@@ -615,7 +615,7 @@ impl Iterator for DmarStructures<'_> {
         }
         let kind = u16(self.body, self.at);
         let len = u16(self.body, self.at + 2) as usize;
-        if len < 4 || self.at + len > self.body.len() {
+        if len < 2 || self.at + len > self.body.len() {
             return None;
         }
         let e = &self.body[self.at..self.at + len];
